    {
      "text": "because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold, Matt. 24:12 (D&C 45:27; JS—M 1:30). where sin abounded, grace did much more abound, Rom. 5:20. Shall we continue in sin, that grace may abound, Rom. 6:1. peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, Rom. 15:13. always abounding in the work of the Lord, 1 Cor. 15:58. sufferings of Christ abound in us, so our consolation also aboundeth, 2 Cor. 1:5. as ye abound in every thing, … see that ye abound in this grace, 2 Cor. 8:7. God is able to make all grace abound toward you, 2 Cor. 9:8. abounded toward us in all wisdom and prudence, Eph. 1:8. in the faith, … abounding therein with thanksgiving, Col. 2:7. abound in love one toward another, 1 Thes. 3:12. if these things be in you, and abound, 2 Pet. 1:8 (D&C 107:31).",
